<title>TURKEY: Turkey's 6th beet test shows 6.13 T/ha sugar.</title>
<headline>Turkey's 6th beet test shows 6.13 T/ha sugar.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Turkey's sixth beet test, carried out on August 30, showed a drop to 6.13 tonnes of sugar per hectare from 6.23 tonnes at the same point in 1995, Turkey's state sugar refineries Turkseker said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said average sugar content was 14.7 percent, up from 14.6 percent in the previous year's corresponding test.  </p>
<p>Turkey holds beet tests at 15-day intervals. Data for the fifth test came from 28 refineries throughout the country.</p>
<p>Details follow.</p>
<p>			     6th test 96    6th test 95    5th test 96</p>
<p>Sugar weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)     6.130	    6.230	    4.870</p>
<p>Average sugar</p>
<p> content (pct)	     14.7	     14.6	     14.0</p>
<p>Number of beets</p>
<p> per hectare		 78,600	   82,680	   78,600</p>
<p>Root weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)    41.640	   42.670	   34.800</p>
<p>Ratio of leaf</p>
<p>weight to beet weight</p>
<p> (leaf/beet)		  0.68	     0.59	     0.76</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
